  "id": "natural-experiment",
  "term": "natural experiment",
  "definition": "A natural experiment is a research design that compares people or groups living in different real-world conditions that are not assigned by the researchers, in order to study how those contrasting environments relate to outcomes. It is used to strengthen causal inference when stable, long-term differences in exposure help establish that exposure came before the measured effect.",
